course: dictionary
lesson: 10737
title: Upset: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word upset can mean different things, so context tells you which meaning you need. Read the words around it. «Mum was upset, then hugged him» means she felt unhappy or worried, because something bad had happened.
explain: Upset can also mean to make someone feel this way. «A lie that upsets people» means the lie makes people unhappy or hurt. Upset can also mean to knock something over or spoil it, as in «upset a cup» or «upset the plans».
explain: Upset can be a noun in sport. An upset is a surprising result where the weaker team wins. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Upset means unhappy, worried or hurt because something bad happened.
fact: To upset someone is to make them unhappy or worried.
fact: To upset something is to knock it over or spoil it: «upset a cup», «upset the plans».
fact: An upset stomach is a mild illness of the tummy, and you may need to rest and drink water.
fact: In sport, an upset is a surprising result where the weaker team wins.
exercise: «Mum was upset, then hugged him and said "thank you for telling me".» What does upset mean here? | Surprised by a win | Very hungry | Knocked over | *Unhappy and worried
exercise: In «upset a cup», what does upset mean? | To make someone feel sad | A surprising sports result | A mild illness of the tummy | *To knock it over
exercise: «In the UK people value queuing very highly, and jumping the queue makes them upset.» What does upset mean here? | Tidied up | Spoiled by a sports result | *Unhappy, worried or hurt | Pleased and happy
test: In sport, what is an upset? | The team that always wins | A sad goodbye after a match | A game that is cancelled because of rain | *A surprising result where the weaker team wins
test: «An upset stomach» means what? | *A mild illness of the tummy | A cross word to a friend | A full, happy belly | A hard fall on the stairs
exam: In «a prank... is not "just a joke" if it upsets people», what does upsets mean? | Knocks people over | Makes people laugh together | Spoils a plan for a party | *Makes people feel unhappy or hurt
